==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|doutless}} {{qualifier|obsolete}}

===Etymology===
From {{suffix|en|doubt|less}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈdaʊ̯tləs/|lang=en}}
* {{a|Canada}} {{IPA|/ˈdʌʊ̯tləs/|lang=en}}
* {{audio|en-us-doubtless.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|-}}

# Characterized by or experiencing no [[doubt]] at all, [[certain]]; [[undoubted]]; [[undoubting]].
#* '''1880''', B. Stewart and P. G. Tait, ''The Unseen Universe'', Macmillan (London), p. xiii:
#*: There are those who have '''doubtless''' faith in revelation.
#* {{quote-text|lang=en|year=1927|author=[[w:Edgar_Rice_Burroughs|Edgar Rice Burroughs]]|title=The Outlaw of Torn|chapter=7|passage=It is '''doubtless''' that the old reprobate who sued for his daughter's hand heard some unsavory truths from the man.}}
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} Free from fear or suspicion.
#* Shakespeare
#*: Pretty child, sleep '''doubtless''' and secure.

