===Adverb===
{{en-adv|-}}

# Without doubt; very [[probably]], [[in all likelihood]]; [[doubtlessly]].
#* '''1893''', [[w:Ambrose_Bierce|Ambrose Bierce]], "The Realm Of The Unreal":
#*: I cannot remember that I spoke a word, though '''doubtless''' I did.
#* '''1900''', {{w|L. Frank Baum}}, {{w|The Wonderful Wizard of Oz}}:
#*: The men, Dorothy thought, were about as old as Uncle Henry, for two of them had beards. But the little woman was '''doubtless''' much older. Her face was covered with wrinkles, her hair was nearly white, and she walked rather stiffly.
#* {{quote-journal
|lang=en
|date=June 26, 2017
|author=Alexis Petridis
|title=Glastonbury 2017 verdict: Radiohead, Foo Fighters, Lorde, Stormzy and more
|work=the Guardian
|url=https://www.theguardian.com/music/2017/jun/26/glastonbury-2017-verdict-radiohead-foo-fighters-lorde-stormzy-and-more
|page=
|passage=Thom Yorke’s onstage pronouncements became less abstract and more effusive, they played the songs the less committed audience members '''doubtless''' wanted to hear in the first place: Paranoid Android, Creep, Fake Plastic Trees and Karma Police. At the end of the latter, Yorke happily led an audience singalong.}}

